From 634576142c63263a50e52d5d6e5f8cee9844035c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bero <bero@lindev.ch>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 00:30:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add in-tree mimalloc2 (v2) backend (--with-malloc=mimalloc2)

Track Microsoft mimalloc v2 under malloc/mimalloc2/ as a selectable
backend alongside mimalloc (v3).  Sources, shims, configure/Makefile
wiring, docs, and v2-vs-v3 benchmark notes.
---

diff --git a/MALLOC-BACKENDS.md b/MALLOC-BACKENDS.md
index a276d19b..9c9e9181 100644
--- a/MALLOC-BACKENDS.md
+++ b/MALLOC-BACKENDS.md
@@ -21,7 +21,8 @@ Currently supported values:
 | Value              | Description                              |
 |--------------------|------------------------------------------|
 | `glibc`            | (default) Traditional ptmalloc2-based allocator |
-| `mimalloc`         | Microsoft's mimalloc, compiled in-tree from `malloc/mimalloc/` |
+| `mimalloc`         | Microsoft mimalloc **v3**, from `malloc/mimalloc/` |
+| `mimalloc2`         | Microsoft's mimalloc, compiled in-tree from `malloc/mimalloc/` |
 | `mimalloc-secure`  | Same mimalloc sources with `MI_SECURE=4` (guard pages, encoded freelists, double-free checks); symbols renamed so it can coexist with `mimalloc` |
 | `jemalloc`         | Facebook/Meta's jemalloc, compiled in-tree from `malloc/jemalloc/` |
 | `snmalloc`         | Microsoft Research's snmalloc, compiled in-tree from `malloc/snmalloc/` |
@@ -227,7 +228,8 @@ Configure variables written to `config.make`:
 
 | Variable          | Single build     | Multi build                          |
 |-------------------|------------------|--------------------------------------|
-| `malloc-impl`     | `mimalloc` etc.  | `multi`                              |
+| `malloc-impl`     | `mimalloc`         | Microsoft mimalloc **v3**, from `malloc/mimalloc/` |
+| `mimalloc2` etc.  | `multi`                              |
 | `malloc-impls`    | one name         | space-separated enabled names        |
 | `malloc-default`  | that name        | `--with-default-malloc` or first     |
 | `malloc-multi`    | `no`             | `yes`                                |
@@ -661,3 +663,38 @@ backend was selected.
 - **Static linking**: All backends are compiled into `libc.a` directly.
   The weak stubs in `elf/static-stubs.c` allow libgcc_eh to be linked
   when needed (e.g. by unwinding paths pulled in transitively).
+
+## mimalloc v2 vs v3 (glibc-style embedding)
+
+Compared by compiling the same amalgamation path glibc uses
+(`static.c` + thin `mi_*` → `malloc` shim, `MI_DEBUG=0`,
+`-O3 -fPIC -fno-gnu89-inline`) and loading via `LD_PRELOAD`.  This
+matches the in-tree backends `mimalloc` (v3.4.5) and `mimalloc2` (v2.4.5).
+Averaged over 3 runs (scale=4).  Times in seconds (lower is better).
+
+| test | mimalloc2 (2.4.5) | mimalloc (3.4.5) | glibc ptmalloc | 3/2 | 2 vs pt | 3 vs pt |
+|------|------------------:|-----------------:|---------------:|----:|--------:|--------:|
+| many_small | 0.020 | 0.027 | 0.066 | 1.35 | 0.30× | 0.41× |
+| mixed_sizes | 0.034 | 0.039 | 0.176 | 1.15 | 0.19× | 0.22× |
+| calloc_free | 0.013 | 0.018 | 0.035 | 1.35 | 0.38× | 0.51× |
+| realloc_grow | 0.005 | 0.006 | 0.002 | 1.27 | 2.50× | 3.17× |
+| churn_frag | 0.014 | 0.014 | 0.045 | 1.05 | 0.30× | 0.32× |
+| threads_1 | 0.005 | 0.007 | 0.018 | 1.50 | 0.25× | 0.38× |
+| threads_4 | 0.013 | 0.013 | 0.024 | 0.95 | 0.56× | 0.54× |
+| threads_8 | 0.024 | 0.021 | 0.052 | 0.90 | 0.46× | 0.41× |
+| threads_16 | 0.042 | 0.041 | 0.089 | 0.97 | 0.47× | 0.46× |
+
+**Summary:** both beat stock ptmalloc on almost all microbench paths.
+v2 (`mimalloc2`) is faster single-threaded; v3 (`mimalloc`) is
+competitive or slightly better under multi-thread load.  `realloc_grow`
+favours ptmalloc.  Date: 2026-08-06.
+
+### Building with mimalloc2
+
+```sh
+../configure --prefix=/opt/glibc-mi2 --with-malloc=mimalloc2 --disable-werror
+```
+
+Same integration as `mimalloc`, but using the **v2** sources under
+`malloc/mimalloc2/`.  Both can be multi-backends (`GLIBC_MALLOC_IMPL=mimalloc`
+vs `mimalloc2`).
